Subject: Cantor Succeeding SOP Fixture Persistence P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] fb244d8c-dd31-4ea4-99ee-1cd51790c813
@ [canonical_uuid] b87c0711-1151-438e-a2eb-35375e88b134

& [WhyNow]
  + B1 remains blocked by the unchanged selected host schema while SWA-06B2A already supplies the complete deterministic input for a later physical writer
  + a fixture-only persistence kernel closes real filesystem mechanics without inventing live activation authority

& [WhyThisBoundary]
  + synthetic_fixture_only prevents generic evidence from being mistaken for governed activation
  + explicit root marker no .git link denial and exact receipt-derived paths sharply bound contact
  + no CLI prevents ambient invocation while the kernel is first verified
  + stopping before boot and rollback keeps post-replacement recovery as an independently reviewable seam

& [ExpectedValue]
  + Cantor gains executable source reacquisition current-registry persistence and current-selection mechanics usable by later independently governed activation orchestration
  + fault state and durable receipts make the physical hemisphere inspectable instead of hiding it behind semantic plans
